      'Turn-flow example: Deal 10 cards to each player and 2 face-down to the prikup. Players bid by passing or naming a trump suit (Paston, Glitch, Dineri, Gupa, Paston grkha). Highest bidder becomes declarer, takes the prikup, discards two cards, and names trump. Declarer must take at least six tricks. Opponents may say whist (defend) or pass. Play: declarer leads; follow suit if possible, otherwise play a trump. Highest trump or highest card of led suit wins the trick; winner leads next. Scores are cumulative; game ends at 121 points.',
      'Scoring example: Cumulative points per round; declarer scores +10 for six or more tricks, -10 for five or fewer; defenders score by tricks taken; multipliers apply for non-spade trumps. First player to reach 121 cumulative points wins..',
